<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">

  {{/* Where fragments contribute to the page. A fragment renders inside the
       <body>, long after this <head> was written, so it cannot put anything
       here by itself — it declares with rc.Hoist and the engine substitutes
       it here once the tree has finished. The pages in home.go hoist their
       own <title>, and a plugin such as collage-jsonld puts its structured
       data here too. Without this marker, everything hoisted has nowhere to
       land and nothing appears. */}}
  {{hoist "head"}}

  {{/* asset resolves this to "/static/app.<hash>.css", which is served with a
       year-long immutable lifetime: a changed file is a changed URL, so the
       browser never has to ask whether its copy is still good. Linking
       "/static/app.css" by hand also works, but can only be cached briefly. */}}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{asset "/static/app.css"}}">
</head>
<body>
  {{slot "content"}}
</body>
</html>
